WEBVTT

00:00:00.620 --> 00:00:03.941
This section is about using
stress management strategies

00:00:03.981 --> 00:00:08.900
to cope with issues when stressful
situations cannot be changed.

00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:15.180
If you are taking this course, you most
likely are experiencing tinnitus symptoms.

00:00:15.320 --> 00:00:18.312
You may have, at some
period of time, felt anger,

00:00:18.352 --> 00:00:21.580
frustration, or even rage
about having tinnitus.

00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:22.957
That is understandable,

00:00:22.997 --> 00:00:28.240
because it is a condition that you
probably do not like nor want to have.

00:00:28.540 --> 00:00:33.203
For the most part, the onset of tinnitus
symptoms is out of your control,

00:00:33.243 --> 00:00:37.960
but you have other areas of control
related to your tinnitus symptoms.

00:00:38.120 --> 00:00:41.527
You have an ability to adjust
your sound environment, as we taught

00:00:41.567 --> 00:00:45.579
in the audiological section,
by adding sounds to your sound environment,

00:00:45.619 --> 00:00:49.148
how much you pay attention
to your tinnitus should decrease.

00:00:49.560 --> 00:00:53.960
You also have control over how you
react to the fact of having tinnitus.

00:00:54.180 --> 00:00:58.860
That is why we want to teach you stress
management strategies in this section.

00:00:59.140 --> 00:01:02.600
These strategies are represented
by a blue toolbox.

00:01:02.880 --> 00:01:06.466
We want to give you more tools
or techniques to reduce your stress

00:01:06.506 --> 00:01:10.680
when you cannot change the fact
of having tinnitus symptoms.

00:01:12.140 --> 00:01:14.439
This is a reminder about the FIT technique

00:01:14.479 --> 00:01:18.260
that is important when you
are choosing coping strategies.

00:01:18.540 --> 00:01:23.700
For effective coping, you must match
the type of coping strategies you use.

00:01:23.880 --> 00:01:25.714
These would be stress
management strategies

00:01:25.754 --> 00:01:28.760
when a stressful situation
cannot be changed.

00:01:29.040 --> 00:01:33.980
Please note that stress management
strategies are active strategies.

00:01:34.020 --> 00:01:38.316
However, instead of trying to solve
a problem that is causing stress, stress

00:01:38.356 --> 00:01:43.620
management strategies focus on changing
your reactions to the stressful situation.

00:01:43.900 --> 00:01:48.720
Here are some ideas about how
to manage your stressful reactions.

00:01:49.880 --> 00:01:53.118
No doubt you already have
found ways to get your mind off

00:01:53.158 --> 00:01:57.120
issues that have bothered you
in various stages of your life.

00:01:57.440 --> 00:01:59.390
Maybe you have been using
some of the following

00:01:59.430 --> 00:02:01.640
kinds of stress reduction activities.

00:02:02.300 --> 00:02:06.380
Involvement in hobbies like woodworking,
mechanics, boating, hunting,

00:02:06.420 --> 00:02:12.064
cooking, gardening, or volunteering,
or spending time with family and friends,

00:02:12.104 --> 00:02:16.951
or interacting with pets,
or exercising such as going for a walk or jog

00:02:16.991 --> 00:02:22.000
or doing aerobics or working out,
or watching movies or television.

00:02:22.620 --> 00:02:27.640
Think about one thing you do to calm
down when something really upsets you.

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:31.500
That is one of your own
coping strategies for stress.

00:02:32.560 --> 00:02:35.659
You probably already have
many stress management skills

00:02:35.699 --> 00:02:40.140
and a certain style that you use
to manage the stress in your life.

00:02:40.420 --> 00:02:42.368
There are many kinds of things people do

00:02:42.408 --> 00:02:45.900
to decrease their reactions
to stressful situations.

00:02:46.300 --> 00:02:49.480
Your way of handling stress
can be highly personal.

00:02:49.520 --> 00:02:54.640
That is fine, but note some more
possibilities for reducing stress.

00:02:55.140 --> 00:03:00.380
Using humor, making light of the situation,
confiding in someone else.

00:03:00.620 --> 00:03:04.720
Looking on the bright side,
following spiritual pursuits.

00:03:06.100 --> 00:03:10.140
Here are some more things people
do to reduce their stress.

00:03:10.640 --> 00:03:15.400
Using so-called mall therapy or retail
therapy, buying things to feel better.

00:03:15.700 --> 00:03:22.040
Taking drugs, drinking alcohol,
smoking cigarettes, overeating.

00:03:22.960 --> 00:03:26.853
Note that while these five strategies may
help give an immediate sense of reducing

00:03:26.893 --> 00:03:31.128
your stress levels, there may be
consequences of using these techniques.

00:03:31.540 --> 00:03:35.816
If these coping strategies become your primary
choices for handling the many types

00:03:35.856 --> 00:03:40.791
of stress you may experience, in health,
work, personal relationships, or finances,

00:03:40.831 --> 00:03:45.540
you may experience greater problematic
or negative outcomes or consequences.

00:03:45.840 --> 00:03:48.820
It is your choice how
you deal with stress.

00:03:49.180 --> 00:03:52.376
This section will cover some
of the main stress management

00:03:52.416 --> 00:03:55.359
strategies so that you can
be more aware of the range

00:03:55.399 --> 00:03:58.940
of choices you have to deal
with stressful situations.

00:03:59.920 --> 00:04:05.086
Most of us do not think very clearly
when we are reacting to stress, but these

00:04:05.126 --> 00:04:09.283
strategies will help you to create
a buffer zone between you and the stress

00:04:09.323 --> 00:04:13.966
that you experience, like a pause button,
so that you are able to think about

00:04:14.006 --> 00:04:19.280
your challenges and plan the types of action
that you can take to change things.

00:04:19.440 --> 00:04:23.240
Sometimes you may use stress
management strategies to calm down,

00:04:23.280 --> 00:04:27.382
pausing to clear your head,
and then you might be able to use

00:04:27.422 --> 00:04:32.880
problem-solving strategies to change
something about a changeable situation.

00:04:34.950 --> 00:04:37.965
Four more strategies that you
can use to reduce your stress

00:04:38.005 --> 00:04:41.064
reactions will be discussed
in the following slides.

00:04:41.110 --> 00:04:46.435
These are physical activity, visualization
and relaxation techniques, also known

00:04:46.475 --> 00:04:52.650
as mindfulness, remembering positive
experiences, and scheduling pleasant events.

00:04:52.950 --> 00:04:57.010
You can use these
strategically to reduce stress.

00:04:58.910 --> 00:05:03.170
Physical activity is one coping
strategy that many people use.

00:05:03.490 --> 00:05:06.255
Physical activity and exercise
help to manage stress,

00:05:06.295 --> 00:05:08.770
clearing your head and boosting your mood.

00:05:08.810 --> 00:05:13.268
It generates physiological changes
in your body, such as releasing endorphins,

00:05:13.308 --> 00:05:16.850
that can help improve your mood
and help clear your mind.

00:05:17.250 --> 00:05:19.173
As we have mentioned
in the previous section,

00:05:19.213 --> 00:05:23.010
we may have a fight-or-flight
response when under stress.

00:05:23.670 --> 00:05:26.990
Exercise is one way to work
with those responses or energy.

00:05:27.030 --> 00:05:29.746
When you exercise,
you flush out stress hormones

00:05:29.786 --> 00:05:33.702
that are circulating in your body
from the various sources of stress,

00:05:33.742 --> 00:05:37.150
such as your tinnitus,
job, relationship problems.

00:05:37.410 --> 00:05:39.448
With these stress hormones flushed out,

00:05:39.488 --> 00:05:43.330
you are actually more
in control of your reactions.

00:05:43.370 --> 00:05:46.590
Also, after exercising your body, i.e.

00:05:46.630 --> 00:05:50.312
your heart rate,
blood pressure and breathing cycle,

00:05:50.352 --> 00:05:53.650
often resets at a lower resting rate.

00:05:53.710 --> 00:05:58.330
Thus, there are multiple benefits
of exercising as a way to manage stress.

00:05:58.870 --> 00:06:02.450
Think about the kinds
of exercises you enjoy.

00:06:02.850 --> 00:06:06.650
What do you notice about
your tinnitus when you are exercising?

00:06:07.230 --> 00:06:10.263
Another stress management
strategy that you can

00:06:10.303 --> 00:06:13.970
initially use is called
positive experiences.

00:06:14.330 --> 00:06:17.767
This strategy involves thinking
back over the past week or two about

00:06:17.807 --> 00:06:22.350
something you did or something that happened
to you that made you feel good.

00:06:22.490 --> 00:06:24.670
This could be an activity, an event,

00:06:24.710 --> 00:06:28.030
or something else that helped
you get through the day.

00:06:28.210 --> 00:06:30.443
So you bring these
positive experiences into

00:06:30.483 --> 00:06:33.550
your awareness and remember
how good you felt.

00:06:33.990 --> 00:06:36.723
Remembering those positive
experiences is important

00:06:36.763 --> 00:06:40.730
because our minds tend to focus
on negative events, i.e.

00:06:40.770 --> 00:06:42.070
negative stimuli.

00:06:42.290 --> 00:06:47.230
And for many humans, there is a repetitive
or exclusive focus on negative events.

00:06:47.310 --> 00:06:51.245
So, intentionally recalling recent
positive experiences can help you

00:06:51.285 --> 00:06:55.818
to balance your sense that while there
are some stressful aspects in your life,

00:06:55.858 --> 00:06:59.870
there are also some positive
things that have recently happened.
